                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2836135,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "He wrote a surprisingly well regarded paper, claiming that birds migrate to the moon and back every year.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 237.05501,
                  "from": 229.14,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2836154,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "He came to this conclusion as the only logical explanation for the total disappearance of some species. One of the key moments in the development of migration theory came in 1822, when a white stork was shot in Germany. This particular stork made history because of the long spear in its neck, which incredibly had not killed it. Everyone immediately realized this spear was definitely not European. It turned out to be a spear from a tribe in Central Africa.",
            "children": [
              {
