                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2836363,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "This idea came about because it seemed impossible that small birds, weighing only a few grams, could fly over vast oceans. This idea was supported by observations of bird behaviour, such as the harassment of larger birds by smaller birds. The development of bird ringing by a Danish school teacher, Hans Christian Cornelius Mortensen, made many discoveries possible. This is still common practice today, and relies upon what is known as recovery. This is when ringed birds are found dead in the place they have migrated to, and identified.",
