            "content": "<h3><strong>Bird Migration Theory</strong></h3>\n<p>Most birds are believed to migrate seasonally.</p>\n<p><strong>Hibernation theory</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; It was believed that birds hibernated underwater or buried themselves in <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_31\">______</span> .</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; This theory was later disproved by experiments on caged birds.</p>\n<p><strong>Transmutation theory</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Aristotle believed birds changed from one species into another in summer and winter.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &ndash;&nbsp; In autumn he observed that redstarts experience the loss of <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_32\">______</span> and thought they then turned into robins.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &ndash;&nbsp; Aristotle&rsquo;s assumptions were logical because the two species of birds had a similar <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_33\">______</span>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>17th century</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Charles Morton popularised the idea that birds fly to the <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_34\">______</span> in winter.</p>\n<p><strong>Scientific developments</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; In 1822, a stork was killed in Germany which had an African spear in its <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_35\">______</span> .</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &ndash;&nbsp; previously there had been no <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_36\">______</span> that storks migrate to Africa</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Little was known about the <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_37\">______</span> and journeys of migrating birds until the practice of ringing was established.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &ndash;&nbsp; It was thought large birds carried small birds on some journeys because they were considered incapable of travelling across huge <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_38\">______</span> .</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &ndash;&nbsp; Ringing depended on what is called the &lsquo;<span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_39\">______</span>' of dead birds</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; In 1931, the first <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_40\">______</span> to show the migration of European birds was printed.</p>",
